  "notes": "Labels use GPIO names from the diagram callouts with the CircuitPython name first in functions; header silkscreen spellings (5V, 3V, 10) added where they differ. The board has a USB-C port at the top and two USB-A host ports at the bottom; the USB-C port was used as the USB connector for pin-order rule 4. Skipped: MicroSD, ESP32 co-processor and I2S/peripheral signals, buttons, LED/IR, NeoPixels, headphone jack, the DVI/HSTX video port (signal list without contact positions) and the USB HOST signal list (USB_HOST_DATA_PLUS/MINUS, USB_HOST_5V_POWER, GND), which belong to USB/video ports rather than wiring points. Speaker callout says 4-8 ohm speaker."
